"'''Don't Turn Around'''" is a [[Popular music|popular song]] written by [[Albert Hammond]] and [[Diane Warren]]. It was originally recorded by American singer [[Tina Turner]] and released as the [[A-side and B-side|B-side]] to her 1986 [[Hit song|hit single]] "[[Typical Male]]". It has since been included on Turner's [[compilation album]] ''[[The Collected Recordings: Sixties to Nineties]]'' (1994), as well as featuring in the ''[[Tina (musical)|Tina]]'' [[Jukebox musical|musical]] since 2018.

The song has been [[Cover version|covered]] by numerous artists, most notably by [[Luther Ingram]] in 1987, [[Aswad (band)|Aswad]] in 1988, [[Bonnie Tyler]] in 1988, [[Jeff Scott Soto|Eyes]] in 1990, [[Neil Diamond]] in 1991, [[Ace of Base]] in 1993, and Albert Hammond in 2010.

